X:05
T:We'll have A Widing What Ever Come out. TCo.05
B:Rev T. Cowper MS, 1766, Westmoreland
Z:Village Music Project 2016 Hugh Taylor
T:A Wedding What Ever Comes Out, aka.TCo.05
N:The time signature appears to be written as Cut Time, but 9/8 seems more obvious.
N:A version of William Vickers in the Great Northern Tune Book also has the same metrical problem. That version
N:has 6 bar A & B written in 6/8, and Matt Seattle has also suggested that it should be 4 bars of 9/8.
N:NB1 - This triplet has the B note barred as quaver
N:NB2 - This bar is written as 'ABc B4 G3 Bc'
N:NB3 - This bar is written as 'ABA f6 A2 ABc'
N:NB4 - This bar is written as 'ABc B4 F4 (or could be G4'
M:9/8
L:1/8
Q:1/2=60
K:G
"_Time signature C| in MS"GAB gfe dBG|"^NB1"ABA f3 AAB|GAB gfe dcB|"^NB2"ABc B3 GBc|
dBd ece dcB|"^NB3"ABA f2A ABc|dBd ece dBG|"^NB4"ABc B3 G3|]

