X:07
T:Brave Capt. Death. TCo.07
B:Rev T. Cowper MS, 1766, Westmoreland
Z:Village Music Project 2016 Hugh Taylor
N:Captain William Death was an 18th century privateer from Middlesex, England who died in battle December 1756
N:in the first year of the Seven Years War. Presumably this is the tune of the song about him
N:No time signature written
N:NB1 - This note looks like it is written as a crotchet
N:NB2 - This G could be an A
N:NB3 - This bar looks like it is written as "e2 ce d3 B2 z G"
N:NB4 - This bar is written as '(A/B/c) BA d2'
N:NB5 - This note is written as an undotted crotchet. I've made it dotted to fit in with the previous bar
M:None
L:1/8
Q:1/2=60
K:G
D2|"_No time sig in MS"G2 FG A2 Bc|d2 BG A3 B|c2 (c/d/e) ~d2 cB|cBAG "^NB1"d3 d|
e2 ce d2 Bd|c2 Ac B3 d|e2 (e/f/g) E2 FG|A>B (c/B/A/G/) F3 D|
"^NB2"G2 AB c2 BA|d2 ef g3 f|"NB3"e2 ce d>B zG |"^NB4"(A/B/c) BA d2|
(e/f/g) gg G3 G|(B/c/d) dd  "^NB5"D3 D|E2 GA Bd dc|"End" B2 cA G4|]

